mdcat-b6-eng-14.qHtml:
Read the passage and answer the question:
&quot;The emergence of multidrug-resistant pathogens represents one of the most perilous global health threats of our century. Overuse and misuse of broad-spectrum antimicrobials in clinical practice and veterinary agriculture have exerted intense selective pressure, accelerating the dissemination of plasmid-mediated resistance cassettes among bacterial populations.&quot;
What is the primary factor identified by the author as driving antibiotic resistance?

mdcat-b6-eng-16.qHtml:
Read the short excerpt:
&quot;Immune checkpoint inhibitors have revolutionized modern oncology by uncoupling the molecular inhibitory pathways that tumors exploit to escape T-cell cytotoxicity. However, this immune liberation frequently engenders immune-related adverse events (irAEs), wherein normal host tissues become innocent victims of auto-reactive T-cell infiltration.&quot;
What can be inferred regarding the adverse effects of immune checkpoint inhibitors?

