&quot;Vaccine-induced herd immunity functions as an immunological shield for individuals who cannot be medically immunized, such as neonates or patients undergoing aggressive chemotherapy. When a critical threshold of the population acquires protective neutralizing antibodies, chains of infectious transmission are effectively severed.&quot;

